            <ArticleTitle>Off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting in a patient with congenital factor V deficiency: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital factor V deficiency is an uncommon bleeding disorder that necessitates hemostatic correction before surgery. We herein describe a patient with severe factor V deficiency who underwent successful off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting with a transfusion of fresh-frozen plasma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
